# Akiba's Beat (PCSG00952, Japanese: Circle confirms): boot, opening movie, title, New Game settings, the event movie
# skipped, then the first minutes of the first delusion dungeon (walk, camera, attacks, the first battle and its tutorials, pause); every step waits for
# the screen; run with VITASHARP_DISPLAY_IMMEDIATE_PACE=1 (Unity flips immediately: unpaced headless it runs at ~460 fps)
# run: VitaSharp.Desktop --data=<root> run PCSG00952 --headless --nav=tests/nav/akibas_beat_start.nav --nav-out=<dir>
log boot
sleep 12
stable 2 90
shot 01_unity
sleep 40
shot 02_opening
press start
sleep 5
shot 03_title
press circle
sleep 3
shot 04_menu
press circle
sleep 4
shot 05_newgame
press start
sleep 3
shot 06_confirm
press up
sleep 1
press circle
log loading, then the opening events: each one is skipped (Start, "Yes" is above "No")
sleep 45
shot 07_event
press start
sleep 3
shot 08_skip
press up
sleep 1
press circle
sleep 15
shot 09_dungeon
sleep 3
shot 10_dungeon
log gameplay: walk, turn, camera, the three attacks, pause
lstick 0 -1 120
shot 11_walk
lstick 1 0 40
lstick 0 -1 120
shot 12_walk
rstick 1 0 60
shot 13_camera
press square
wait 15
shot 14_square
press triangle
wait 15
shot 15_triangle
press circle
wait 15
shot 16_circle
lstick 0 -1 240
shot 17_walk
log the first enemy: the encounter opens a battle with tutorial boxes (Circle closes each)
sleep 4
shot 18_battle
press circle
sleep 2
press circle
sleep 2
press circle
sleep 2
press circle
sleep 2
shot 19_tutorials
press square
wait 15
press square
wait 15
press square
wait 15
shot 20_attack
lstick -1 0 60
press square
wait 15
press triangle
wait 15
shot 21_attack
press circle
sleep 2
press circle
sleep 2
lstick 1 0 60
press square
wait 15
press square
wait 15
sleep 5
shot 22_battle
press start
sleep 2
shot 23_pause
press start
sleep 2
press circle
sleep 2
press square
wait 15
press square
wait 15
sleep 10
shot 24_later
quit